 ### PlaNeRF
-PlaNeRF is an unsupervised 3D plane regularization method for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) designed to improve large-scale urban scene reconstruction. It addresses the geometric instability of NeRF in low-texture, flat-surface environments by appending two regularization terms to the standard L2 photometric loss: a patch-based SSIM term for geometry initialization and an SVD-based plane regularization term for enforcing planar geometry. Unlike sibling methods such as [RegNeRF](link-to-regnerf) which enforce a plane orthogonal to the center ray, PlaNeRF targets the least-squares plane approximation of a patch, allowing the surface normal to converge in an unsupervised manner.
