 ### GeCoNeRF
-GeCoNeRF is a regularization framework for few-shot Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) optimization that enforces geometric consistency across views using depth-guided warping and feature-level consistency modeling to overcome under-constrained optimization and overfitting. It sets itself apart from pixel-level photometric consistency methods (e.g., NeuralWarp, StructNeRF) by operating at the feature level, which preserves view-dependent specular effects that pixel-level losses would suppress. Unlike pre-training-based few-shot methods (e.g., PixelNeRF, MVSNeRF), it optimizes NeRF from scratch without requiring extensive multi-scene dataset priors.
+GeCoNeRF is a regularization framework for few-shot Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) optimization that enforces geometric consistency across views using depth-guided warping and feature-level consistency modeling to overcome under-constrained optimization and overfitting [S1]. It sets itself apart from pixel-level photometric consistency methods (e.g., NeuralWarp, StructNeRF) by operating at the feature level, which preserves view-dependent specular effects that pixel-level losses would suppress [S1]. Unlike pre-training-based few-shot methods (e.g., PixelNeRF, MVSNeRF), it optimizes NeRF from scratch without requiring extensive multi-scene dataset priors [S1].
 
 ### [Lambertian Augmentation](8108-lambertian-augmentation.md)
-Lambertian Augmentation is a regularization technique used within the Simple-RF framework to mitigate shape-radiance ambiguity and duplication artifacts in radiance field optimization. It addresses the problem where NeRF models with limited input images exploit view-dependent color variations to explain observed images, leading to incorrect geometry. By constraining an augmented, lower-capacity version of the model to output Lambertian (view-independent) colors, it provides a simpler ground truth that guides the main model toward correct geometric structures.
