 ### SinNeRF Loss and Annealing Strategy
 This variant applies a specific loss annealing strategy to the Simple-RF framework [S2]. The overall loss function is:
 $$ \mathcal{L}_{\text{total}} = \mathcal{L}_{\text{pix}} + \lambda_1 \mathcal{L}_{\text{geo}} + \lambda_2 \mathcal{L}_{\text{adv}} + \lambda_3 \mathcal{L}_{\text{cls}} $$
-where $\lambda_1, \lambda_2, \lambda_3$ are weighting factors [S2]. The weights are annealed during training: initially, $\lambda_1 = 8$, $\lambda_2 = 0.1$, and $\lambda_3 = 0$ [S2]. During the training process, $\lambda_2$ is gradually decreased to 0 and $\lambda_3$ is increased to 0.1 with a linear function [S2].
